<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech power firm plans higher '96 dividend.</title>
<headline>Czech power firm plans higher '96 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech regional power utility Prazska Energetika a.s. said on Tuesday it would propose a 25 crown gross dividend per share on 1996 earnings, up from 20 crowns the previous year.</p>
<p>&quot;Gross dividend should be 2.5 percent of the (1,000 crown) nominal value,&quot; a company representative said.</p>
<p>The Prague-based regional electricity distributor posted a preliminary 1996 net profit of 362 million crowns, after 455 million in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
